(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #130: a field is written by the same rule as a
 variable. A text that is not a number, cast into a number field or a
 float field, raises the error flag and leaves the field as it was; one
 that is a number is stored.)

A thing called point has
  a number called x is 9,
  a float called weight is 1.5.

a point called origin.
a text called word is "hello".
a text called digits is "42".
Set origin's x to word as a number.
On error print "x kept".
Set origin's weight to word as a float.
On error print "weight kept".
Print origin.
Set origin's x to digits as a number.
origin's weight is digits as a float.
Print origin.
